/-!
# `row_residue` for q = 3 through `ZMod 11`

`vSeedPrime 3 = 11`.  Data (all checked exactly in Python, see `checks/`):
* `q3rzD r` is the lcm of the denominators of row `r` of
  `q3SourceMatrixAtZeroExplicit`; `q3rzN0 = diag(q3rzD) * M_0` and
  `q3rzAN = diag(q3rzD) * A` are integer matrices, so
  `diag(q3rzD) * M_t = q3rzN0 - t * q3rzAN`;
* for `t = 0..4`, `q3rzE * q3rzNbar_t = q3rzL_t * q3rzU_t` in `ZMod 11`, with
  `q3rzE` upper and `q3rzL_t` lower unitriangular, and `q3rzNbar_t` the residue of
  `q3rzN0 - t * q3rzAN`;
* `q3rzW` inverts the Vandermonde matrix `(tʲ)` modulo 11.

No rational determinant at `T ≠ 0`, no rational interpolation, and no 9 by 9
Leibniz expansion occurs.  Every `decide` acts on entries below 11, on one
`ℤ → ZMod 11` cast, on one 9-term dot product, or on the product of nine
small naturals.  Determinants are reached only through `Matrix.det_mul`,
`Matrix.det_of_isUpperTriangular`/`isLowerTriangular` and `RingHom.map_det`.
Exact coefficient residues: [1, 4, 6, 7, 1] = `vSeedResidueRow 3`.
-/

namespace Li2Lean.B3

noncomputable section

open Li2Lean
open Matrix

set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 20000000

instance q3rzFact : Fact (Nat.Prime (vSeedPrime 3)) := ⟨by norm_num [vSeedPrime]⟩

